{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1394749-homebrewed-legacies","id":1394749,"title":"Homebrewed Legacies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-07T04:07:12-07:00","id":1394749,"title":"Homebrewed Legacies","content":"Went reading through my Changeling book again, and got an urge to try homebrewing some custom Legacies for characters to follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>UNSEELIE LEGACIES:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Heretic:</b> The Unseelie court is filled with rebels and dissidents who scoff at the rules of conventional society, but their acts of defiance are often limited to causing trouble on a more personal level. The heretic seeks to shake things up on a much broader scale, by convincing everyone else to join in! They can often be found among various activist groups, where they rise to the ranks of leadership, or at least become recognized as very enthusiastic members. They are among the most dangerous kind of rebels, for they possess a magnetic charisma that others find difficult to resist.<br /> <br /> <b>Quest:</b> When you convince others to challenge the established dogma, regain a point of willpower.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Never allow yourself to be swayed by common rhetoric.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cursed Beauty:</b> Ugly on the outside, sweet on the inside; there are many fairy tales about innocent men and women who were cursed with a form that many others would consider to be revolting. Often at times, these curses were meant to encourage others to overcome their prejudices and see beyond the common stereotype. Some tales claim that the curse may be lifted if the victim managed to find true love, but others had a tendency to end in tragedy.<br /> <br /> <b>Quest:</b> When someone acknowledges your more subtle virtues instead of the more overt flaws, regain a point of willpower.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Never judge somebody based on face value.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>NIGHTMARE LEGACIES:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Wishmaster:</b> Many are the tales which warn mortals to be careful what they wish for, and such tales involving fairies are even more cautionary. The wishmaster has a talent for giving people what they ask for, but it is almost never in the manner the recepient expected it to happen. A couple wishing for a child might receive a chimerical infant who never ages, while someone wishing for money might receive a sizeable inheritence after the tragic death of a loved one. Wishmasters seem to derive pleasure from corrupting the desires of their clients, fulfilling the letter of the wish, but not the spirit of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Urge:</b> When you make somebody regret getting what they want, regain a point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Taboo:</b> Never attempt a genuine effort to make someone else happy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Warrior:</b> A soldier fights to live, but a warrior lives to fight. Nothing is more boring to the warrior, than a life without conflict; preferably that of the physical kind. A true warrior has a reputation for glorifying their battle scars, and considers death by combat to be the greatest honor that one may achieve. Because of this, they are almost impossible to intimidate, and actively seek out mighty foes to pit themselves against.<br /> <br /> <b>Quest:</b> When you physically defeat an opponent who's power rivals your own, regain a point of willpower.<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Never participate in cowardly, indirect tactics to win battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","user":"NewNyrufa","date":". 06-07-2020, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26211-newnyrufa","name":"NewNyrufa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}